# Instruction-set envelope for milestone 3.
# ceiling  : the widest registers this milestone's reference uses.
# field    : a dispatch field this milestone installs through.
# returnfile: a file whose `return X;` names an installed kernel.
# sym      : a symbol the reference's own files define.
# ownfile  : a file this milestone owns, named relative to libswscale/x86/.
#            The envelope gate is scoped to what the candidate changed: every
#            ownfile byte-identical to the base's passes it vacuously and the
#            verifier prints that it did. The Makefile is deliberately not an
#            ownfile -- it is shared bookkeeping that earlier milestones also
#            edit, so counting it would report a cumulative candidate as
#            having changed this milestone's scope when it changed nothing of
#            this milestone's.
ceiling avx2
enforce no
# This milestone has no `field` to scrape and no `returnfile` to read: the
# fused-operation backend is a table of callbacks (`const SwsOpBackend
# backend_x86`), so its dispatch installs kernels by assigning struct members,
# not by assigning a SwsContext field or returning a name. Without a seed the
# gate resolved to no object at all and reported `MILESTONE_OBJECTS 0` on
# every tree -- an examination that found nothing, kept from being a failure
# only because this milestone's ceiling equals the machine's (`enforce no`).
# The symbols this milestone's own files define seed the scope instead, so the
# gate follows and reports the objects that implement this milestone.
sym backend_x86
sym ff_sws_process1_x86
sym ff_sws_process2_x86
sym ff_sws_process3_x86
sym ff_sws_process4_x86
ownfile ops.c
ownfile ops_common.asm
ownfile ops_float.asm
ownfile ops_include.asm
ownfile ops_int.asm
ownfile uops_macros.asm.h
